   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Naming furniture",
     "texto": [
      "Rooms and pieces of furniture take en or et depending on their gender: en stol, et bord. The definite form adds an ending: stolen («the chair»), bordet («the table»).",
      "Det er is used to say «there is» or «there are», with one thing or with several: Det er en stol («there is a chair»), Det er to stoler («there are two chairs»). Unlike English «there is» and «there are», er does not change with the number."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
